# Borough alerts. Installed at /etc/cron.d/rentmap-alerts (scp this file;
# never hand-edit on the box — see deploy/cron-rentmap-growth).
#
# Every 10 minutes: refresh Housing Connect, welcome new sign-ups, mail what
# is new. "The minute a lottery opens" is a promise about THIS cadence — the
# Housing Connect refresh is one cheap POST and the run is a no-op when
# nothing changed, so ten minutes costs nothing.
#
# One email a day per address, across every job (growth/mailcap.py). Since
# 2026-10-06 only Find A Crib Plus subscribers are sent the moment something
# opens (push at once, email while the day's slot is free); everyone else's
# matches are held for the 8 AM --digest below.
#
# Replaces the twice-daily /etc/cron.d/rentmap-housingconnect: the wrapper
# writes the same housing_connect.json, so that file is removed on install.
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
*/10 * * * * scraper fac-run supabase,smtp,apns -- /root/Find-A-Crib/lottery_alerts.sh >> /var/log/rentmap-alerts.log 2>&1

# Below here the clock is New York's. The 8 AM digest comes first so it holds
# the day's one email; the nudge, the weekly round-up and the 08:20
# saved-building run (deploy/cron-rentmap-saved) follow it.
CRON_TZ=America/New_York

# 8 AM: the daily digest for subscribers without Plus (2026-10-06). It runs
# first so it holds the day's one email; the nudge and weekly moved after it.
0 8 * * * scraper fac-run supabase,smtp,apns -- /root/Find-A-Crib/lottery_alerts.sh --digest >> /var/log/rentmap-alerts.log 2>&1
# 08:35 daily: first-week round-up for sign-ups that have had only the welcome.
35 8 * * * scraper fac-run supabase,smtp,apns -- /root/Find-A-Crib/lottery_alerts.sh --nudge >> /var/log/rentmap-alerts.log 2>&1

# 08:40 Tuesdays: the weekly round-up — opened this week, closing this week.
40 8 * * 2 scraper fac-run supabase,smtp,apns -- /root/Find-A-Crib/lottery_alerts.sh --weekly >> /var/log/rentmap-alerts.log 2>&1
